 "model_choice": "Position Encoding TSP (n^2 variables). Rationale: The specification requires a closed tour visiting every station exactly once. Position encoding (x[i,t] = 1 if station i is at position t) naturally enforces 'visit each station once' and 'each position has one station' via simple linear constraints. Crucially, it inherently prevents subtours because the sequence is linear with a wrap-around edge, satisfying the 'single tour' requirement without auxiliary MTZ variables. Size: For N stations, variables = N^2. With N ~ 45-60, N^2 is approx 2,025 - 3,600. This fits within the CGA backend limit of ",
